      "problem": "Simplify $\\sqrt{12x}-\\sqrt{27x}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We simplify each of the radical terms using the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{12x}-\\sqrt{27x} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{4\\cdot 3x}-\\sqrt{9\\cdot 3x} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{3x}-\\sqrt{9}\\cdot \\sqrt{3x} & = \\\\ 2\\cdot \\sqrt{3x}-3\\cdot \\sqrt{3x} & = \\\\ 2\\sqrt{3x}-3\\sqrt{3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we combine like terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{3x}-3\\sqrt{3x} & = \\\\ (2-3)\\cdot \\sqrt{3x} & = \\\\ (-1)\\cdot \\sqrt{3x} & = \\\\ -\\sqrt{3x}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
